ive attachment unchanged. The 14-module focused selection passed 318/318. Independent review, full make verify, Gerrit votes, and merge remain pending.","timestamp":1792776451091398416},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Signed Group23 candidate 31ed99d034f982593fa2ca3ef970d4d927345305 (Change-Id Ia0c431e8080b7242383d4cc491407add89d3ee1e) changes exactly 112 scoped reconciler prose blocks. Historical d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84 before and signed-HEAD after citations are in the external author draft. Local structural audit: 112/112 shorter, 7,366→1,860 words, executable AST/directives unchanged. The 14-module focused selection passed 318 tests; make lint, commit hooks, and every non-full registered DD pass. Non-author review, full make verify, Gerrit votes, and merge are pending.","timestamp":1792777243135267661},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Citation correction for signed Group23 candidate 31ed99d034f982593fa2ca3ef970d4d927345305: all 112 independent-review before citations and before_words must use the actual current parent `cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a:tests/unit/reconciler/...` blocks. The historical d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84 paths remain scope provenance only. The refreshed author TSV now has 112/112 exact cbc before citations, 7,311→1,860 words, all strict reductions, and 0 structural audit errors. Signed source is unchanged.","timestamp":1792777384538195942}],"created_at":1788572119807296620,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c4f2080e-09ce-4057-9c17-f8e5b7b80f4d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e236-b04a-3798-4a09"},{"link_uuid":"bc15ffcc-2a3c-4ccf-9486-b62b2c79a59d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3c6e-ba88-ae16-49f5"},{"link_uuid":"9ca11c1f-1c02-4d93-b223-a7d1f8bccdbd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b102-053c-3bd8-4e95"},{"link_uuid":"1e597215-05cb-400f-a782-2104867ee19c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e146-9d7a-cd04-4dce"},{"link_uuid":"70cc955f-75f2-47f9-83b5-91d90f8b5fdd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6820-b590-f2d3-4460"},{"link_uuid":"6549a9c3-87f1-4e9c-bc3a-4f97b6c2cc25","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ff1a-3546-60dd-449e"},{"link_uuid":"e012959f-f637-4dc1-a595-9e84cd9095a8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"746f-4df7-6e62-43c0"},{"link_uuid":"4aa709ea-ba89-4a06-887a-516d901499a0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"067e-d415-fac1-4a04"},{"link_uuid":"c97a0cdf-bdb3-4705-a5fa-bc394f4a36ad","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e032-af86-60c7-40f9"},{"link_uuid":"6d4bace7-9ce4-4135-90b8-dad8fc8349e9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8994-a548-9f97-4098"},{"link_uuid":"15a521e4-108c-4933-bae0-7dafa974adea","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6703-f711-c7d8-45b5"},{"link_uuid":"fb744fe2-60f2-449f-ac4b-596b31804c4f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fa98-3988-5cbb-4f32"},{"link_uuid":"0a1e8fa8-ccc8-4005-aa84-d4f8708e9bab","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ffd5-d4a0-0918-414d"},{"link_uuid":"f8a66089-dcfc-4dfb-b4d1-d54262fc1b25","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f1ef-616a-0a5d-44e2"},{"link_uuid":"33727e39-8ea1-47a7-8769-063831cf4bb7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5d71-c299-4ff7-4e34"},{"link_uuid":"f675ef71-d23d-4240-b280-3ea86b3f475d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5698-c28d-fdda-4132"}],"description":"## Context / immutable basis\nExactly 112 surviving bloated prose blocks are confirmed in 14 live paths under tests/unit/reconciler/; the 7 blocks in test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py and 1 block in test_timeout_s_forwarding_heldout_7504.py were deleted on current main. Condense redundant or historical text while retaining non-obvious contracts.\n\nHistorical audit `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84` records the original `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` provenance. The 14 surviving files moved to `tests/unit/reconciler/`. Implement from `origin/main@cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a`; every review-row before citation and word count uses that exact current parent path/block. The same cbc tree supplies the executable AST/directive comparison base. The grouped commit has 32 changed paths.\n\n## Boundary and guards\nEdit only the anchored ordinary comments/docstrings below and adjacent blank lines. Currentize RED, pre-fix, “Today”, and implementation-scaffolding prose. Executable statements, assertions, runtime strings, directives, and unlisted prose stay unchanged.\n\nParse base/final files with ast.parse(source, type_comments=True); strip only leading Expr(Constant(str)) nodes from Module/ClassDef/FunctionDef/AsyncFunctionDef bodies; normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno; require exact ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False) equality. Tokenizer comparison preserves exact directive text/attachment; runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n\n## Scope — 112 editable blocks\n- test_rich_text_codec.py (7) — module; test_{over_limit_text_is_fitted_and_marked,wiki_over_limit_value_ends_with_the_marker_and_fits_the_cap,adf_over_limit_value_ends_with_the_marker_within_the_serialized_cap,normalize_outbound_equals_decode_of_to_wire}; comments beginning “Both codecs append” and “The codec law”. Preserve caps, terminal markers, and codec law.\n- test_rich_text_cutover.py (6) — module and the five immutable-basis test_* docstrings of at least 35 words from test_codec_law_holds_in_both_modes through test_resolver_lives_in_the_shared_layer_without_cloud_imports.\n- test_rich_text_echo_suppression.py (4) — module and test_{lossy_baseline_compare_local_normalized,legacy_body_upgrades_once,cutover_does_not_mass_rewrite_already_synced_bodies}. Preserve lossy-wire convergence and one-time upgrade.\n- test_run_differs_recovery_no_write.py (3) — module, _seed_keyed_pending, test_live_pass_still_performs_recovery_writes. Preserve preview/dry-run zero-write and live contrast.\n- test_run_pass_lock_lost_exit.py (4) — module, _lock_lost_cls, test_lock_lost_mid_pass_exits_reschedule_not_error, test_generic_failure_still_exits_one. Preserve keyed exception identity and exit 75/1 split.\n- test_transition_replay.py (28) — module; comment beginning “Lazy imports of the module under test”; helpers _write_status_event, _make_tracker, _point_config_at, _FakeTransport; and the 22 immutable-basis test_* docstrings of at least 30 words from test_replay_resume_point_matches_in_jira_name_space through test_recorded_hops_for_reads_self_resolved_store. Replace lazy-import RED history; preserve hop ordering, resume, drift, and transient propagation.\n- test_transport_exception_contract_heldout.py (7) — module and all six test_* docstrings from test_backend_http_error_subclasses_urllib_http_error through test_no_core_module_names_a_vendor_exception. State the implemented adapter-neutral exception, deletion, and soft-degradation contract.\n- test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py (4) — module, test_{the_only_deliberate_any_is_the_runtime_guard_itself,the_port_is_importable_from_any_core_module_without_a_cycle}, and comment beginning “The ONE deliberate”. Preserve resolvable port typing and its sole exemption.\n- test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py (12) — module, the 10 immutable-basis test_* docstrings of at least 35 words from test_dc_transport_exposes_every_member_the_core_calls through test_a_successful_dc_reporter_write_leaves_the_next_differ_pass_clean, and comment beginning “What DC hands back”. Preserve port census, identity shape, pagination, construction guards, logging, and idempotence.\n- test_type_mapping.py (12) — module and all 11 immutable-basis test_* docstrings of at least 29 words, from test_effective_type_map_default_equals_builtin through test_local_type_vocab_derived_from_ticket_type. Preserve map parity, SKIP, fail-closed behavior, and label round-trip.\n- test_user_identity_heldout.py (5) — module; test_data_center_{is_authoritative_for_a_resolvable_assignee,converges_on_the_second_pass}; test_identity_models_discover_no_collaborator_by_getattr; comment beginning “assignee resolution is the OUTBOUND role”. Preserve resolver injection and identity distinctions.\n- test_wiki_render_corpus.py (5) — module; test_{dc_corpus_protected_excerpts_are_retained,dc_corpus_passes_two_to_five_are_byte_identical,dc_corpus_coverage_ratios}; comment beginning “NOTE: there is deliberately NO test”. Preserve code excerpts, convergence, richness floors, and corpus-vocabulary boundary.\n- test_wiki_render_hardening.py (10) — module; test_{a_non_positive_timeout_falls_back_rather_than_disabling_rendering,a_config_object_without_the_key_falls_back_rather_than_raising,a_timeout_reaps_the_whole_process_group_not_just_the_child,the_child_leads_its_own_process_group,the_unit_is_delivered_on_stdin_with_the_landed_argv,an_empty_stdin_would_have_been_detectable,static_replay_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer}; comments beginning “A REAL executable” and “Separates \\\"the 1s timeout”. Preserve bounded/reaped subprocess behavior, stdin delivery, and golden replay.\n- test_write_ahead_recovery.py (5) — module, test_keyless_pending_miss_unbinds, test_coordinated_abort_leaves_keyed_pending_recovered_without_search; comments beginning “The unbind lands on the THIRD miss” and “A bare MagicMock answers”. Preserve corroborated absence and create/label recovery ordering.\n\n## Consumers and directives\nPytest collects every module; check_comment_hygiene.py consumes repository prose. No targeted __doc__, inspect.getdoc, or doctest consumer was found.\n\nPreserve exactly 23 directive tokens/attachments: codec 2 arg-type; cutover 3 arg-type; echo 2 pragmas; lock-lost 1 no-any-return; exception 4 arg-type; typing 1 pragma; completeness 6 attr/method ignores; type-map 1 arg-type; wiki 1 reap pragma; write-ahead 1 union-attr plus 1 must-not-call pragma.\n\n## Independent receipt\nA non-author reviewer posts exactly 112 leaf-linked TSV rows:\npath<TAB>anchor/kind<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session\n\nCitations use full SHAs, every after count is lower, and both verdicts are PASS. Missing, duplicate, or extra rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] TSV has 112 unique rows, one per allowlisted block.\n- [ ] Each row cites full before/after SHAs.\n- [ ] Each row has `after_words < before_words`.\n- [ ] Each row has `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] Each row has `semantic-preservation=PASS`.\n- [ ] Each row has `directives_exact=PASS`.\n- [ ] Each `reviewer-session` names a non-author.\n- [ ] DD `semantic` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `directives` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `paths` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `diff` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `hygiene` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `focused` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `full` exits 0 without a timeout.\n\n## Verification\nRun all seven structured commands: semantic, directives, paths, diff, hygiene, focused, full.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py","reason":"Condense codec law/cap prose while preserving terminal markers, serialized limits, and normalization."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py","reason":"Condense cutover prose while preserving both send paths, codec law, optional-dependency fallback, and layer ownership."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_echo_suppression.py","reason":"Condense echo-suppression prose while preserving lossy normalization, one-time upgrade, and no mass rewrite."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_differs_recovery_no_write.py","reason":"Condense recovery-mode prose while preserving preview/dry-run zero writes and live recovery contrast."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_pass_lock_lost_exit.py","reason":"Condense lock-loss prose while preserving keyed exception identity and exit-75 versus exit-1 classification."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_transition_replay.py","reason":"Replace stale lazy-import/RED history and condense replay oracles while preserving hop ordering, resume, drift, and transient errors."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_exception_contract_heldout.py","reason":"Currentize held-out transport-exception prose while preserving adapter-neutral deletion and soft-degradation behavior."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py","reason":"Condense transport-typing census prose while preserving resolvable port annotations and the sole Any exemption."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py","reason":"Condense port-completeness oracles while preserving member census, identities, pagination, construction guards, logging, and idempotence."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_type_mapping.py","reason":"Condense type-map test prose while preserving map parity, SKIP, fail-closed behavior, and label round-trip."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_user_identity_heldout.py","reason":"Condense identity-model prose while preserving declared resolver injection and Cloud/DC authority distinctions."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py","reason":"Condense corpus prose while preserving protected code excerpts, convergence, richness floors, and vocabulary boundaries."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","reason":"Condense renderer-hardening prose while preserving bounded group reaping, stdin delivery, fallbacks, and golden replay."},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_write_ahead_recovery.py","reason":"Condense write-ahead recovery prose while preserving corroborated absence and create/label/pending ordering."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","bea4-b9cc-18cc-40c4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"bea4-b9cc-18cc-40c4","parent_status_uuid":"723d59fb-ea82-40b5-a4c5-9e366c784ee7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"a4db-90b9-9488-4ab5","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit/reconciler — cohort 06: rich_text_codec–write_ahead_recovery","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import ast, subprocess, sys\nBASE=\"cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a\"\nclass StripDocstrings(ast.NodeTransformer):\n    def generic_visit(self, node):\n        node = super().generic_visit(node)\n        if isinstance(node, (ast.Module, ast.ClassDef, ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)) and node.body and isinstance(node.body[0], ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value, str):\n            node.body = node.body[1:]\n        if isinstance(node, ast.TypeIgnore):\n            node.lineno = 0\n        return node\ndef normalized(raw):\n    return StripDocstrings().visit(ast.parse(raw, type_comments=True))\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    before = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", BASE + \":\" + path], text=True)\n    after = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", \"HEAD:\" + path], text=True)\n    if ast.dump(normalized(before), include_attributes=False) != ast.dump(normalized(after), include_attributes=False):\n        raise SystemExit(\"normalized AST changed: \" + path)' tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_echo_suppression.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_differs_recovery_no_write.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_pass_lock_lost_exit.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transition_replay.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_exception_contract_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_type_mapping.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_user_identity_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_write_ahead_recovery.py","dd_id":"semantic","dd_text":"Every impacted Python file has an exactly equal normalized AST against the current cbc02f0e execution base."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import io, re, subprocess, sys, tokenize\nBASE=\"cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a\"\nPATTERN=re.compile(r\"#\\s*(?:noqa\\b|type:\\s*ignore\\b|pragma:\\s*no cover\\b|fmt:|ruff:|pyright:|mypy:)\")\ndef source(ref, path):\n    return subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", ref + \":\" + path], text=True)\ndef signatures(raw):\n    lines=raw.splitlines()\n    found=[]\n    for token in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(raw).readline):\n        if token.type != tokenize.COMMENT or not PATTERN.match(token.string):\n            continue\n        row, col = token.start\n        left=lines[row - 1][:col].rstrip()\n        anchor=(\"inline\", left) if left else (\"next\", \"<EOF>\")\n        if not left:\n            for line in lines[row:]:\n                stripped=line.strip()\n                if stripped and not stripped.startswith(\"#\"):\n                    anchor=(\"next\", stripped)\n                    break\n        found.append((token.string, anchor))\n    return found\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    if signatures(source(BASE, path)) != signatures(source(\"HEAD\", path)):\n        raise SystemExit(\"directive text or attachment changed: \" + path)' tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_echo_suppression.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_differs_recovery_no_write.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_pass_lock_lost_exit.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transition_replay.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_exception_contract_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_type_mapping.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_user_identity_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_write_ahead_recovery.py","dd_id":"directives","dd_text":"Every protected directive retains exact token text and executable attachment."},{"command":"rtk proxy env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import subprocess, sys\nexpected=sorted(sys.argv[1:])\nactual=sorted(subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD^..HEAD\"], text=True).splitlines())\nif actual != expected:\n    raise SystemExit(\"changed paths differ from file impact: actual=\" + repr(actual) + \" expected=\" + repr(expected))' tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_echo_suppression.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_differs_recovery_no_write.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_run_pass_lock_lost_exit.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transition_replay.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_exception_contract_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_type_mapping.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_user_identity_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_write_ahead_recovery.py .github/workflows/_artifact-probe.yml .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml .github/workflows/_eval-discipline.yml .github/workflows/_mutation.yml .github/workflows/_optionality.yml .github/workflows/codeql.yml .github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml .github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.